In article <41601@lanl.gov> bxb@lanl.gov (barry j. berenberg) writes:
>Here's what may be a better solution:  wands aimed at the ground (>)
>create a trap.  These traps can either be permanent or of a finite
>duration.  Whether the wand is blessed/uncursed/cursed makes a
>difference:

A while back, I was thinking along similar lines.  But, what if traps were
created by applying a wand, and then setting it down on (or throwing it
toward) the desired spot for the trap?  A wand with more charges would
be more likely to work.  In any case, that wand would be gone.  On
occassion, an applied wand might mis-fire.  Certain dangerous wands
(like death) should not, however, mis-fire in a deadly way.

>	WAND			TRAP
...
>	death			death (perm)

No, please, no death traps.  If the ability to make traps is added to the
game, there should be a chance to find any such trap that we could create.
Besides, this could be abused in shops.

Richard Addison


